~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Second, independent opinion on the drugs ranked by the machine-learning model. The top 15
  candidates         from step 05, plus the reference/control drugs, are physically docked into
  the TgDHFR active site with AutoDock Vina:         each molecule is converted to 3D, many
  positions/orientations are tried inside the search box, and the best-scoring         poses are
  kept (3 per drug). ML looks at chemical similarity to known inhibitors; docking looks at 3D
  shape/chemical fit to the real protein pocket, so agreement between the two is stronger evidence
  than either alone.
  Docking score (kcal/mol): more negative = predicted tighter binding. Rule of thumb used here:
  below -8.0         = binding confirmed. Scores are approximate (errors of 1-2 kcal/mol are
  normal) and rank-ordering is more reliable         than absolute values. LE here is score per
  heavy atom (more negative = more efficient binder).
  'Agreement' column: VALIDATED (+) = ML says active (pIC50 > 6.5) AND docking confirms; VALIDATED
  (-) =         both say inactive; ML FALSE POSITIVE = ML active but docking does not confirm; ML
  FALSE NEGATIVE = the reverse;         Neutral = in between. Energy_Gap_P1_Pn is how much worse
  the 3rd pose is than the 1st (small gap = several similar         alternative poses, i.e. a less
  defined binding mode). Max_RMSD_UB is how different the extra poses are (Å).         Limitation:
  the receptor is rigid and water/protonation states are not modelled.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

