[EXPLAIN] Reading the benchmark
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  'R2 ± std' is the mean and spread of R2 over the cross-validation folds; the 95% CI is the range
  in which the true         performance is expected to fall. Compare it with the classical R2
  values drawn as dashed lines in the figure. Large         std or a wide CI means the result
  depends strongly on which molecules landed in the test fold (typical for small data).
  The scatter plot (right panel of the figure) shows predicted vs. experimental pIC50: points on
  the diagonal are perfect         predictions; systematic curvature at the extremes means the
  model compresses very high/low potencies toward the mean.
