~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Two extreme potencies were removed from the main dataset (outside the Tukey fences of the pIC50
  distribution). Here the         nested-CV benchmark run WITH them (sensitivity/) is compared
  with the main run, representation by representation, and a         Morgan/Random Forest model
  trained without them is asked to predict them. If the scores barely move and the model
  predicts the extremes badly, they are unrepresentative of the series (outliers) but harmless to
  the conclusions; if the         scores change materially, the exclusion is a modelling choice
  that must be reported.
